ok - --config preserves configured mode
ok - searchd -c/--config -e uses configured binary and HTTP listeners
ok - searchd -e uses the normally discovered config when no local instance exists
ok - searchd -e never falls back past an existing local data marker
ok - bare searchd preserves default configuration lookup
ok - searchd -l creates manticore_data with HTTP Unix socket and no TCP listeners
ok - searchd -e executes SELECT and semicolon-separated queries
ok - searchd -e supports vertical output with \\G
ok - searchd -e frames terminal output with timing and preserves redirected TSV
ok - Buddy callbacks use the local Unix socket
ok - local Buddy startup skips the sharding plugin
ok - interactive completion expands SQL keywords, tables, and columns
ok - interactive history persists and terminal interrupts clear the draft
ok - concurrent clients merge bounded plain-text history and preserve invalid files
ok - searchd -e supports interactive exit, EOF, and persistent session state
ok - interactive mode reports errors and continues with the next line
ok - duplicate local startup does not disturb the current directory instance
ok - searchd -e preserves semicolons inside strings
ok - searchd -e handles comments without corrupting arithmetic or batch boundaries
ok - searchd -e rejects unterminated block comments without executing their SQL prefix
ok - searchd -e preserves signed 64-bit integer precision
ok - searchd -e renders JSON null as NULL
ok - searchd -e stops a batch on the first SQL error
ok - searchd -l --stopwait targets the local daemon only
ok - local DDL/DML persists across restart
ok - local and configured daemon lifecycles stay isolated
